                if crc & 0x80:
                    crc = (crc << 1) ^ poly
                else:
                    crc <<= 1
        return crc & 0xFF

if __name__ == "__main__":
    dht20 = DHT20()
    temperature, humidity, crc_error = dht20.measure()
    if crc_error:
        print("Error reading data")
    else:
        print("Temperature: {}°C".format(temperature))
        print("Humidity: {}%".format(humidity))
```
This code defines a `DHT20` class that interfaces with the DHT20 sensor on I2C bus 1. The constructor opens the bus and verifies the sensor by reading the status register. The `measure` method initiates a reading, polls the status register roughly every 10 ms until the data is ready or a total timeout of 0.1 second is reached, extracts the 20-bit humidity raw value from bytes 1-3 and the 20-bit temperature raw value from bytes 3-5, computes the CRC-8 checksum using the documented polynomial and initial value over the first six bytes, and finally returns a tuple `(temperature, humidity, crc_error)` with the converted values on success or `(None, None, True)` on failure. Any I/O failure when opening the bus or verifying the sensor must be logged and cause `self.bus` to be set to `None`. The program handles SIGINT and SIGTERM gracefully by closing the I2C bus on exit. The `__main__` block takes a single measurement and prints the result.

