This code defines a `RotaryEncoder` class that takes the GPIO pins for the CLK and DT signals, as well as an optional callback function to be called on each rotation. The class sets up the GPIO pins and adds event detection for both signals, using a debounce interval of 0.005 seconds. The `_clk_callback` and `_dt_callback` methods are called on each rising and falling edge of the CLK signal, respectively, and they update the counter value based on the current DT state and the previous CLK state. The `cleanup` method is called on exit to safely close the GPIO pins.

The `__main__` block sets up an instance of the `RotaryEncoder` class and runs an infinite loop that sleeps for 0.005 seconds. The `KeyboardInterrupt` exception is caught to gracefully exit the program and release all resources.

